  "body": "Fire a bubbling, composed, cancelable `focusreset` event (using `FocusResetEvent`) when focus is involuntarily reset to a `Document`'s viewport because the focused area was removed from the DOM (`#node-remove-focus-fixup`) or stopped being a focusable area (`#focus-fixup-rule`, e.g. `disabled`, `hidden`, `inert`, `display: none`), and focus has not since been moved to another focusable area.\n\n- **Target**: Dispatched at the element itself if still connected, or at the nearest surviving connected ancestor (`Element`, `ShadowRoot`, or `Document`) when the focused node (or an ancestor) was removed. If a surviving ancestor is later removed before rendering, `pending focusreset target` walks up to the new surviving ancestor and retargets `pending focusreset related target`.\n- **`FocusResetEvent.relatedTarget`**: Exposes the `Element` that lost focus, retargeted against `currentTarget` (with disconnected shadow-tree candidates falling back to retargeting the shadow host when `currentTarget` is outside the shadow root).\n- **Timing**: Dispatched in `update the rendering` immediately after `#focus-fixup-rule`, coalescing multiple focus resets within the same frame and only firing if the document still has focus and no ongoing `navigate` event is handling focus reset automatically.\n\nFixes #12842.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63595\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/572677865\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2081188\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327387\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/876\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n/dom.html ( [diff](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/html/13050/eb68265...f1e74a4/dom.html) )\n/infrastructure.html ( [diff](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/html/13050/eb68265...f1e74a4/infrastructure.html) )\n/interaction.html ( [diff](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/html/13050/eb68265...f1e74a4/interaction.html) )\n/nav-history-apis.html ( [diff](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/html/13050/eb68265...f1e74a4/nav-history-apis.html) )\n/webappapis.html ( [diff](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/html/13050/eb68265...f1e74a4/webappapis.html) )\n/indices.html ( [diff](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/whatwg/html/13050/eb68265...f1e74a4/indices.html) )\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13050/dom.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:52 PM UTC (f1e74a4)\">/dom.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13050/86190a4...f1e74a4/dom.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:52 PM UTC (f1e74a4)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13050/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:52 PM UTC (f1e74a4)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13050/86190a4...f1e74a4/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:52 PM UTC (f1e74a4)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=